rds did come back after a few days, like uomo after 5 days, though some took too long. Meanwhile certo, tempo, vita, cose, visto, qualcuno, ciao, dio, dopo, adesso, bisogno and amico slipped away and no card asked about them. I'd like those back.","costUsd":0.0066619,"usage":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":290,"cacheReadTokens":2059,"cacheCreationTokens":888}},{"bot":"control-it","week":3,"runId":"38489275236","text":"This week felt uneven. Letter tiles were easy, and I got every one of them right, but the harder cards hit me. I got none of the say-translation, typed-translation, sentence-translation or cloze cards right. Multiple choice went badly too, with only 1 of 4 right. So it was too easy in some places and too hard in others, and the app didn't seem to notice which was which.\n\nI never saw the same word twice in one session, so nothing felt repetitive. Words did return on later days, like proprio after 9 days, volta and qualche after 5, and meglio, signore and modo after 4. That spacing felt about right.\n\nWhat bothered me were the words I forgot that never came back: certo, tempo, vita, cose, visto, qualcuno, ciao, dio, dopo, adesso, bisogno, amico. I saved them and then nothing asked me about them. Also, 2 spoken answers weren't heard, and 6 cards couldn't be matched to a saved word.","costUsd":0.0068898,"usage":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":312,"cacheReadTokens":2058,"cacheCreationTokens":890}},{"bot":"control-it","week":4,"runId":"38630747999","text":"This week I opened the app every single day, and that's the strange part: nothing happened. No sessions, no cards, nothing right, nothing wrong, and no new words saved. So I can't say it was too easy or too hard, because I never got a single question. There was no same word coming back again and again either, and no word returning on a later day.\n\nWhat bothers me is the words I've forgotten and nobody asked me about: certo, tempo, vita, cose, visto, qualcuno, ciao, dio, dopo, adesso, bisogno, amico. These are common words, the kind I need all the time, and they just slipped away with no card to catch them. I'd expect the app to bring them back when I forget them. This week it didn't, and I felt stuck.","costUsd":0.0053735,"usage":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":232,"cacheReadTokens":2175,"cacheCreationTokens":708}}],"progress":{"day":29,"lookups":0,"sessions":0}}
